  "_format": "Scene Objects (v2). Each object: instance_id (unique in this scene), asset_uid (immutable reference into assets/asset_registry.json), x/y = the sprite CONTENT's bottom-center anchor in 1920x1080 scene pixels, scale = uniform render scale of the sprite's native content (always >= 0; horizontal mirroring is the separate flipX flag, default false), z = legacy field (kept for compatibility; no longer drives stacking). Depth: rendering priority is renderLayer (optional int 0..9, fixed band; absent = dynamic) first, then Y-sort by ground line within the band — sortY (optional, scene px) overrides the ground line for props standing ON other props (the record player rests on the cabinet, so it sorts at the cabinet's base, not its own). collision (optional {enabled, offsetX, offsetY, width, height}, scene px, offsets = box top-left relative to the anchor) is the movement-blocking rectangle — a SEPARATE system from depth, absent/disabled blocks nothing. v1 entries ({id, asset, width}) are still accepted by the loader for backward compatibility. Loaded by loadSceneProps() (public/app.js); written by the F8 Scene Editor's Save Layout via POST /api/dev/scene-config."
